{
  "dom_id": "step-q354909",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "At a gourmet shop, a $4$-cup container of artisanal soup costs $$11.20.$ What's the unit price per fluid ounce?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert from cups to fluid ounces. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we multiply the number of cups by $8:$  \n\n$$\n4\\times 8=32\n$$\n\nSo, $4$ cups is the same as $32$ fluid ounces. Now, to find the unit price per fluid ounce, we divide the total price by $32:$  \n\n$$\n11.20÷32=0.35\n$$\n\nTherefore, the artisanal soup costs $$0.35$ per fluid ounce.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
